const FAQS = [["How is the SALU merit aggregate calculated?","The official merit formula is: Pre-Entry Test (or passed HEC USAT score) = 50%, Intermediate (HSC-II) = 30%, and Matriculation (SSC) = 20%."],["What is the passing score on the Entry Test / USAT?","In the SALU Entry Test (out of 50), scores below 17 are considered failed. If applying via HEC USAT, you must score at least 50 out of 100."],["How do I apply online for SALU admissions?","Register on the official portal (www.salu.edu.pk), fill in your academic details, pay the Rs. 2,500/- processing fee challan via HBL Konnect, upload your documents, and submit the printed form with attested copies to the Directorate of Admissions."],["Who can apply for BS Part-III (Bridging)?","Candidates who passed a 2-Year Bachelor (B.A./B.Sc./B.Com.) or Associate Degree (ADE/ADS/ADC) in 2021 or onwards with at least 50% marks."],["Is the HEC Law Admission Test (LAT) required for LLB?","Yes, passing the HEC LAT is mandatory for admission to the 4-Year LLB program at SZAB School of Law."],["Which programs are offered at Ghotki and Shahdad Kot Sub-Campuses?","Both Ghotki and Shahdad Kot Sub-Campuses offer 4-Year BS programs in Business Administration (BBA), Computer Science & I.T., and English Language & Literature."],["What is the Tuition Fee Refund Policy?","100% refund up to the 10th day of classes, 80% up to the 15th day, 60% up to the 20th day, 50% up to the 30th day, and 0% after the 30th day."],["Are hostels and scholarships available for students?","Yes, SALU has 5 Boys Hostels and 3 Girls Hostels (Rs. 14,000/- per year), grants 10% tuition freeships and 2.5% bursaries, and facilitates HEC Need-Based, Ehsaas, SEEF, and Zakat scholarships."]];

